{
  "_what": "How a formula written as text (=PRICE * QUANTITY, IF(@.done, \"yes\", \"no\"), FILTER(items, |x| => x.age > 3)) becomes one composition-ast binding the engine evaluates like any other (src/text.rs). The text is parsed by the formula grammar; each operator and each function is then looked up here, so a name added here is a function at once and the compiler names none. A bare name or @.path reads the row (select self), @@ and $scope read the variables of those names, and a lambda's parameters read the variables its function binds.",
  "_function_row": "name (and aliases) as written, any case; op: the op:core id it runs. input: which argument is the value the op runs on (an index), {list: i} for every argument from i on gathered as one list (one argument that is itself the list stays as it is), or absent for none. args: each op argument name and where its value comes from: an index; {at: i, default: v} for an argument that may be left out; {value: v} for a fixed value; {rest: i} for the arguments from i on as a list; {chain: i, binds: [...]} for a lambda at i, compiled into a chain of steps that starts from the bound value, binds naming the variable each lambda parameter is read from in order ($acc and so on), item_var for the item (named after the parameter and passed as the op's item_var). yields_list: the chain's value is wrapped in a one-item list (for an op that splices what each item makes). example: one text, the row it runs on and the value it gives; the test runs every example through the engine.",
  "_not_carried": {
    "REPLACE": "the old REPLACE(text, start, length, new) replaced by position; no op does that, and SUBSTITUTE replaces by text",
    "DSUM, IS_NUMBER": "left as they are by the coordinator's word (Nov 19 2026): core.sum and core.type_of answer them",
    "CAN, CURRENT_USER, HAS_ROLE, GET_ENTITY, EMIT_EVENT": "access is each pursuit database's own rights, not role lookups in a formula; these wait for a ruling",
    "versioned calls (NAME@v2)": "no user-defined functions exist to version"
  },
  "operators": {
    "binary": {
      "Add": { "op": "op:core.add", "arg": "value" },
      "Subtract": { "op": "op:core.sub", "arg": "value" },
      "Multiply": { "op": "op:core.mul", "arg": "value" },
      "Divide": { "op": "op:core.div", "arg": "value" },
      "Modulo": { "op": "op:core.mod", "arg": "value" },
      "Eq": { "op": "op:core.eq", "arg": "value" },
      "NotEq": { "op": "op:core.ne", "arg": "value" },
      "Lt": { "op": "op:core.lt", "arg": "value" },
      "Lte": { "op": "op:core.le", "arg": "value" },
      "Gt": { "op": "op:core.gt", "arg": "value" },
      "Gte": { "op": "op:core.ge", "arg": "value" },
      "And": { "op": "op:core.and", "values": true },
      "Or": { "op": "op:core.or", "values": true }
    },
    "unary": {
      "Not": "op:core.not",
      "Negate": "op:core.neg"
    },
    "index": { "op": "op:core.lookup", "arg": "key" },
    "value_of": { "op": "op:core.coalesce", "_what": "the one step of a lambda's chain: the value of its body (null stays null)" }
  },
